From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:41:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: add the CONSYS (MT6631) node and its EMI
 reserve

The vendor WMT stack (out-of-tree, patches/wifi in t1100-ubuntu) binds to
mediatek,mt6771-consys and takes all of its addresses from that node: the
CONN MCU window at 0x18070000 (chip id 0x18070008, MCR doorbell, ROM_DESEL),
TOP_RGU 0x10007000 (CPU SW reset), INFRACFG_AO 0x10001000 (AXI bus protect)
and SPM 0x10006000 (CONN power domain, 0x1000632c).

Without the node the driver never probes, and without memory-region it has no
place to put the ROM patch and firmware, so the chip stays in ROM (cpupcr
0x1170, chip id never reads 0x788).

The 2 MiB CONNSYS shared RAM is an alloc-ranges region, not a 'reg': LK spins
forever in reserved_memory_conflict_check when a /reserved-memory child
overlaps a region it reserved itself (docs/lk-dtb-rules.md).

Values match the stock DTB (refs/stock-mt6771.dts) and the MT6771 node in the
Unihertz Titan ALPS tree.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 60 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 60 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index 4d389bd23..3f42cc84c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -756,6 +756,66 @@ &mt6358_vcn33_reg {
 	regulator-boot-on;
 };
 
+/*
+ * CONNSYS (MT6631 combo, CONSYS_6771) — the node the vendor WMT stack binds to.
+ *
+ * Neither mainline 6.12 nor our port has a driver for this block in-tree: it
+ * comes from the out-of-tree vendor stack (patches/wifi/, docs/wifi-port.md).
+ * The node is still needed, because that stack takes everything from it:
+ *
+ *   reg[0] 0x18070000  CONN_MCU_CONFIG  - chip id (0x18070008 = 0x0788), MCR,
+ *                                         WFDMA doorbell, ROM_DESEL
+ *   reg[1] 0x10007000  TOP_RGU          - CPU SW reset (bit 12, key 0x88)
+ *   reg[2] 0x10001000  INFRACFG_AO      - AXI bus protect (0x100012a4)
+ *   reg[3] 0x10006000  SPM              - CONN power domain (0x1000632c)
+ *
+ * The addresses, IRQs and the memory-region shape are the ones the stock DTB
+ * uses (refs/stock-mt6771.dts) and they match the MT6771 node published in the
+ * Unihertz Titan ALPS tree, i.e. they are not guessed.
+ *
+ * Supplies: vcn18/vcn28 - the combo's 1.8 V and 2.8 V rails; vcn33 is already
+ * kept on above (BT/Wi-Fi selector on the shared MT6358 LDO).
+ *
+ * No "conn" clock here on purpose: see above - mainline has no such provider
+ * and listing a phandle that does not exist would only break the build.
+ */
+/ {
+	consys: consys@18070000 {
+		compatible = "mediatek,mt6771-consys";
+		reg = <0 0x18070000 0 0x1000>,
+		      <0 0x10007000 0 0x100>,
+		      <0 0x10001000 0 0x1000>,
+		      <0 0x10006000 0 0x1000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 289 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>,
+			     <GIC_SPI 291 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		vcn18-supply = <&mt6358_vcn18_reg>;
+		vcn28-supply = <&mt6358_vcn28_reg>;
+		vcn33-supply = <&mt6358_vcn33_reg>;
+		memory-region = <&consys_reserve_memory>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * CONNSYS shared RAM: 2 MiB, 2 MiB aligned, no fixed address - the kernel picks
+ * one inside the window the stock DT gives (0x40000000-0xc0000000; the stock
+ * boot landed on 0xbfc00000). It is deliberately an alloc-ranges region and not
+ * a `reg': LK runs reserved_memory_conflict_check over /reserved-memory children
+ * and spins forever if one of them overlaps a region it reserved itself
+ * (docs/lk-dtb-rules.md, and the ramoops note at the bottom of this file).
+ * Without this region the WMT stack has nowhere to load the ROM patch and the
+ * firmware, and the chip never leaves ROM (cpupcr stays 0x1170).
+ */
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	consys_reserve_memory: consys-reserve-memory {
+		compatible = "mediatek,consys-reserve-memory";
+		no-map;
+		size = <0 0x200000>;
+		alignment = <0 0x200000>;
+		alloc-ranges = <0 0x40000000 0 0x80000000>;
+	};
+};
+
 &mt6358regulator {
 	vsys-ldo1-supply = <&reg_vsys>;
 	vsys-ldo2-supply = <&reg_vsys>;
